                  ┌───────────────┐
                  │    Client                   │
                  └───────┬──────┘
                                     │
                           WebSocket
                                    │
                                   ▼
                  ┌───────────────┐
                  │ Load Balancer       │
                  └───────┬──────┘
                                     │
             ┌─────────┴────────────┐
             ▼                                                ▼
      ┌─────────────┐          ┌─────────────┐
      │ Spring Boot       │          │ Spring Boot       │
      │ Instance 1         │          │ Instance 2          │
      └──────┬─────┘          └──────┬─────┘
             │                                                   │
             └────────────┬─────────┘
                                          ▼
                   ┌─────────────┐
                   │    Kafka              │
                   └─────────────┘
But now each application instance maintains:

WebSocket connection
       ↓
Client session
       ↓
Memory of application instance

Therefore, horizontal scaling becomes more complicated.

7. The Most Important HLD Interview Point

The real trade-off is:

Long Polling
Simple
  ↓
Stateless HTTP
  ↓
Easy horizontal scaling
  ↓
Higher HTTP overhead

WebSocket
Persistent connection
  ↓
Lower latency
  ↓
Bidirectional communication
  ↓
Stateful connection management
  ↓
More complex scaling

8. When Would I Choose Which?
Choose Long Polling when:

Updates are relatively infrequent
        +
Simple architecture preferred
        +
Existing HTTP infrastructure
        +
Occasional near-real-time updates
Examples:
	• Job status 
	• Payment processing status 
	• Background task completion 
	• Notification updates 
Choose WebSockets when:

Continuous real-time communication
        +
Very low latency
        +
Bidirectional communication
        +
Many messages
Examples:
	• Chat 
	• Multiplayer games 
	• Trading dashboards 
	• Collaborative editing 
	• Live tracking 
